# Conventions

## Naming

- Files: kebab-case (`create-user.command.ts`, `user.entity.ts`)
- Classes: PascalCase; commands/handlers: `{Action}Command`, `{Action}Handler`
- DTOs: `{Entity}Dto`, `CreateUserDto`, `UserResponseDto`; use `PartialType` for updates
- Ports: `I{Name}Port` + `{NAME}_PORT` Symbol for DI

## Typing

- Strict TypeScript; no `any`. Use explicit return types on public methods.
- DTOs: class-validator decorators (`@IsEmail()`, `@MinLength()`, etc.) + `@ApiProperty()` for Swagger

## Style

- Single responsibility; small functions; avoid deep nesting
- Prefer dependency injection; avoid static/global state in business logic
- Validate at boundaries (DTOs); treat all input as untrusted

## Formatting

- Follow ESLint + Prettier (single quotes, etc.). See `.eslintrc*`, `prettier` config.

## Errors & logging

- Handle errors explicitly; no silent catch. Log with context (e.g. Pino).
- Use NestJS exception filters and validation pipe; see `src/filters/`.
